   dict(key="delhi", to="Delhi", km=250, days="1 to 2 days", road="NH44 via Ambala and Karnal",
    intro="Officers on posting, lawyers and staff moving between the High Court and Delhi, students joining Delhi University and families following a job in the capital keep this one of the busiest short routes out of Chandigarh.",
    about="The truck leaves the Tricity through Zirakpur, crosses the Zirakpur flyover and runs down the Ambala road to meet NH44 near Ambala. From there it is a straight run south on the six-lane highway past Shahabad, Pipli near Kurukshetra, Karnal, Panipat and Sonipat to the Delhi border at Singhu. At about 250 km, the move uses the up to 500 km band of our chart. A dedicated truck loaded in the morning can reach Delhi the same evening, but delivery is usually set for the next morning so the unloading falls inside the city's timings for goods vehicles.",
    dest="Delhi addresses for Chandigarh families tend to be of three kinds: a government quarter in RK Puram, Kidwai Nagar, Netaji Nagar or Lodhi Colony; a builder floor in South or West Delhi, with a small lift or a steep stair; or a DDA flat in Dwarka, Rohini or Vasant Kunj. A verified partner team in Delhi does the unloading and setting up. Older colonies are lined with parked cars, so the truck may stop at the colony gate and goods come in on trolleys. From November to January the GRAP stage in force can bar older diesel goods vehicles from Delhi, so the coordinator picks a vehicle that meets the rules for that week.",
    tip="If you are moving into a government quarter, carry the allotment letter and the possession slip on the day. Many residential campus gates ask to see one of them before a goods vehicle is let in.",
    faqs=[("How long does delivery from Chandigarh to Delhi take?","Most loads reach the next day. A dedicated truck can deliver the same evening if both ends are ready, while a part load on a shared truck may take two days. The coordinator confirms the slot the day before."),
          ("What is the car shifting charge from Chandigarh to Delhi?","On a carrier, roughly Rs 5,500 to 9,000 for a hatchback such as a WagonR, Rs 6,500 to 10,500 for a Dzire or City, Rs 7,500 to 12,000 for a Creta or Nexon and Rs 9,000 to 14,000 for an Innova or Scorpio, plus GST."),
          ("Can you move a hostel or PG room to Delhi University?","Yes. A bed, a table, a few cartons and a cycle are priced as a 1 RK on the up to 500 km band, roughly Rs 8,500 to 15,000 plus GST; a scooter goes on its own line at roughly Rs 2,500 to 4,000 plus GST. Hostels around North Campus often fix move-in hours, so share them early.")],
    photos=["crew/crew-carton-packing-home","crew/crew-carton-shoulder","crew/crew-carton-taping","sp/sp-home-packing-720"],
    more=[
     ("Chandigarh to Delhi packers and movers for postings and studies", [
       "Two cities that run governments trade people all year. Officers of Punjab, Haryana and the UT go on deputation to central ministries, Delhi-based officers come the other way, and lawyers from the Punjab and Haryana High Court in Sector 1 move to practise before the Supreme Court. Students who finish school in Chandigarh head to Delhi University, and parents often rent a flat near North Campus or in Mukherjee Nagar for them.",
       "Most of these are planned around a fixed date: a joining order, a session start or a quarter allotment. Our own crew packs in Chandigarh, usually the day before, and the truck leaves early the next morning so the Delhi partner team can unload in daylight. Because the distance is short, many families also move in two parts, sending the house first and driving down with valuables a day later."]),
     ("Packing for a short highway move", [
       "Five to six hours on NH44 can still shake things loose. Glass tops, mirrors and framed photos are packed in their own cartons with corner guards, the fridge is defrosted the night before, and the washing machine drum is locked. Wooden furniture gets corrugated sheet and stretch film, because a short trip often means more stops and more handling at a builder floor stair.",
       "Since the truck reaches within a day, many people keep plants and kitchen basics to the last carton, so the first meal in Delhi is easy. Every carton carries a room name and a number from the inventory, and the same list is checked at the Delhi door before the partner team signs off."]),
     ("Chandigarh to Delhi shifting charges", [
       "On the up to 500 km band, plus GST: a 1 RK is about Rs 8,500 to 15,000, a 1 BHK Rs 9,500 to 17,000, a 2 BHK Rs 13,000 to 24,000, a 3 BHK Rs 17,000 to 32,000 and a 4 BHK or large kothi Rs 23,000 to 41,000. A Classic 350 or Apache class bike is about Rs 4,000 to 6,000, and a small office of up to 10 workstations about Rs 25,000 to 45,000. Tolls go on the estimate as their own line."])]),
   dict(key="gurugram", to="Gurugram", km=270, days="1 to 2 days", road="NH44 and KMP Expressway",
    intro="Software, consulting and finance staff joining offices in Cyber City, on Golf Course Road and along Sohna Road form most of this route, with Tricity families following a job to the Millennium City.",
    about="Gurugram can be reached without crossing Delhi. The truck runs south on NH44 from Ambala to Kundli, turns onto the Kundli-Manesar-Palwal Expressway, which loops west of Delhi past Bahadurgarh, and leaves it near Manesar to join NH48 into Gurugram. This keeps the load clear of Delhi's goods vehicle timings and its winter restrictions. The trip is about 270 km on the direct road and somewhat more on the expressway loop, well inside the up to 500 km band either way, and goods normally arrive the next day.",
    dest="Most homes at this end are in towers. Societies on Golf Course Extension Road, Sohna Road and in the Dwarka Expressway sectors usually want a move-in form, a truck gate pass and a booked service lift, and many allow shifting only by day. In DLF phases, Sushant Lok and South City, independent floors with narrow stairs are common. A verified partner team in Gurugram handles the unloading. During heavy July and August rain, stretches of NH48 near Hero Honda Chowk can flood quickly, so unloading days in the monsoon are kept flexible.",
    tip="Get the move-in approval from the Gurugram facility office in writing before the Chandigarh loading day, and share the guard-room number with the coordinator. The partner team then calls the gate ahead of arrival.",
    faqs=[("How many days does Chandigarh to Gurugram take?","Usually one day, with unloading the morning after loading. A part load on a shared truck can take two days. You get the driver's number when the truck leaves Chandigarh."),
          ("What does bike shifting from Chandigarh to Gurugram cost?","An Activa or Jupiter goes for roughly Rs 2,500 to 4,000, a Splendor or Pulsar 150 for Rs 3,000 to 4,500, a Classic 350 or Apache for Rs 4,000 to 6,000, and an RE 650 or Duke 390 for Rs 6,000 to 9,000, all plus GST. Each bike is wrapped in foam and cardboard."),
          ("Can you move a small office from the IT Park to Gurugram?","Yes. A team of up to 10 seats moves for roughly Rs 25,000 to 45,000 plus GST, a floor of 10 to 30 seats for roughly Rs 50,000 to 1,00,000 plus GST, and 30 to 100 seats for roughly Rs 1,20,000 to 2,50,000 plus GST. The move is usually done over a weekend.")],
    photos=["crew/crew-carton-packing-home","crew/crew-carton-shoulder","crew/crew-carton-taping","sp/sp-team-truck-1200"],
    more=[
     ("Chandigarh to Gurugram packers and movers: who makes this move", [
       "Chandigarh's IT Park and the Mohali tech offices train a lot of young engineers, and many of them move to the bigger campuses of Cyber City, Udyog Vihar and Golf Course Road after a few years. Engineers also leave for the car and two-wheeler plants around Manesar. A smaller group are Tricity parents moving to Gurugram to live near children who have settled there.",
       "Young professionals usually send a 1 BHK or a shared flat with a bike. Families moving for a senior role tend to bring a full 3 BHK from a Chandigarh kothi or a Mohali society, often with two cars. Knowing the Gurugram tower and floor at survey time lets us size the load to the service lift and the slot the society gives."]),
     ("Fitting a Chandigarh house into a Gurugram flat", [
       "A kothi room is rarely the size of a tower bedroom. Large double beds, heavy almirahs and carved dining sets from the northern sectors may not pass through a Gurugram lift or turn in a flat corridor. At the survey we measure the biggest pieces and compare them with the new flat's door and lift, so anything that will not fit can be sold, given away or opened up in Chandigarh.",
       "Packing follows the layout of the new home rather than the old one. Cartons are marked with the new room name, wardrobes are dismantled with their fittings bagged and taped inside, and mattresses go into thick covers for the lift ride. That keeps the partner team's work inside the society's time window."]),
     ("Chandigarh to Gurugram shifting charges", [
       "Plus GST on the up to 500 km band: about Rs 9,500 to 17,000 for a 1 BHK, Rs 13,000 to 24,000 for a 2 BHK, Rs 17,000 to 32,000 for a 3 BHK and Rs 23,000 to 41,000 for a 4 BHK. On a carrier, a sedan is about Rs 6,500 to 10,500 and a luxury car in an enclosed carrier about Rs 18,000 to 30,000. The written figure after the survey is the figure you pay.",
       "Inside each band, the final figure depends on how much is going, whether you share a truck or book one for yourself, and how long the carry is at each end. A shared load is usually the cheaper choice on this short route because the Tricity to NCR road carries a lot of household loads. A small booking advance holds the date, and the balance is paid after unloading."])]),
