    about="The truck runs south on NH44 to Kundli, follows the peripheral expressway round the west of Delhi and joins NH48 near Manesar. From there the highway crosses Rajasthan through Jaipur, Ajmer and Udaipur, enters Gujarat by the Shamlaji side and passes Ahmedabad, Vadodara, Surat and Vapi before reaching Mumbai. Some loads use the Delhi-Mumbai Expressway for part of the way. At about 1,650 km, the route sits on the 1,500 km plus band of our chart, and a shared truck usually delivers in 6 to 8 days.",
    dest="A Chandigarh family will usually trade floor space for location in Mumbai. A kothi or a 3 BHK in Mohali often becomes a 2 BHK in Andheri, Powai, Thane or Navi Mumbai. Housing societies want a written approval from the secretary before a truck unloads, and many limit shifting to set hours. A verified partner team in Mumbai handles the unloading. Lifts in older buildings are narrow, and from June to September the rain is heavy enough that the entrance and lift are covered before any carton comes off.",
