    about="The truck runs down NH44 to the Delhi region, uses the peripheral expressways to bypass the city and heads to Agra. From Agra it stays on NH44 almost all the way, through Gwalior, Jhansi and Sagar, across Madhya Pradesh to Nagpur and into Telangana through Adilabad and Nirmal, before reaching Hyderabad's Outer Ring Road. The distance is about 1,790 km, which puts the move on the 1,500 km plus band, and a shared truck usually takes 6 to 8 days.",
    dest="Most Tricity families settle in the western suburbs, in Gachibowli, Kondapur, Madhapur, Kokapet or Tellapur, where large gated communities ask for a form, ID copies and a lift booking. A verified partner team in Hyderabad does the unloading. March to May is very hot and the rain falls mostly between June and September. The Outer Ring Road lets trucks reach the western side without entering the old city.",
