    about="This trip crosses most of India. The truck bypasses Delhi, reaches Agra and follows NH44 south through Gwalior, Jhansi, Nagpur and Hyderabad. Below Hyderabad it crosses the dry Rayalaseema country around Kurnool and Anantapur and enters Bengaluru from the north near Yelahanka and Hebbal. At about 2,380 km, the move is on the 1,500 km plus band, the top band of our chart, and a shared truck normally takes 8 to 10 days.",
    dest="Before a truck may unload, most Bengaluru apartment associations want their own form filled in, proof of tenancy or ownership and a lift booking on an agreed date. A verified partner team in Bengaluru handles the unloading. Heavy vehicles face limits on many city roads at busy hours, and the Outer Ring Road near Bellandur and Marathahalli is slow most of the day, so unloading starts early. Rain can come from June to October and sometimes outside it, so covers for the lobby travel with the goods.",
